# This file controls what Docker may copy from the repo root into an image build
# (the Go images use the repo root as their build context). It is an ALLOW-list:
# ignore everything, then re-allow only what a Go build needs. That way .env
# files, .git, node_modules, ai-log.md and the rest can never end up inside an
# image, even if someone adds a broad COPY later.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd/
!internal/
!db/migrations/
